<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masinissa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 238–148 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Massinissa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masinissa was the first king of united Numidia. Son of Gaia of the Massylii, he fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> but went over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 206 BCE, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syphax">Syphax</a> and led the Numidian cavalry at Zama in 202 BCE. He then united Numidia with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirta">Cirta</a>, encouraged farming and towns, and steadily encroached on Carthaginian territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masinissa.jpg" alt="Masinissa" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_of_Masinissa_-_Capitoline_Museum.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
